This product includes software developed as part of the Laminar project.

The JAM notation implemented by this software was originally proposed in:

  Jessica Arcudia, Filiberto Ortiz-Chi, Adolfo Sanchez-Valenzuela,
  Alan Aspuru-Guzik, and Gabriel Merino.
  "Joining and arrangement of multilayers: A string representation for
  honeycomb layered materials."
  Matter, 6(5):1503-1513, 2023.
  doi:10.1016/j.matt.2023.02.014

The canonical filtering formalism implemented in canonjamr is described in:

  Edgar Castillo and Jessica Arcudia.
  "Canonical representation of JAM chains: formalism and a linear-time
  algorithm."
  (manuscript in preparation, 2026).

Laminar is an independent implementation. It is not derived from the
original xJAM codebase.
